=begin
  start_marathon.lic

  Starts ;taskmaster marathon with the outfitting tools, and the stock you
  already have, on hand. If ;stash put any of either away (in your Eddy, or
  the vault), it runs ;unstash marathon first: the outfitting tools, plus one
  piece each of the burlap cloth, rat-pelt leather, wool yarn and cotton
  thread the marathon sews and knits from (not your rare cloths and
  leathers). Every other piece of those four, stashed or in your
  crafting_container, is thrown out: down the vault's garbage chute at the
  vault, else into a bin if the room has one, or dropped. It starts
  taskmaster only once none of the tools are left stashed. Stock that couldn't be got back doesn't stop it, since
  taskmaster buys whatever it's short of.

  taskmaster tops up cloth and leather to 100 yards and yarn and thread to
  400, but COUNTs only one piece of each, so more pieces are only weight.
  (2026-11-26: bringing back 23 of the 31 wool yarns in the vault, most of
  them work order leftovers, made the grey rucksack too heavy for the
  burlap cloth, and taskmaster stopped with cloth it had bought in hand.)
  With nothing to fetch, it combines the pieces of each stock in your
  crafting_container into one, as far as a spool holds.

  Why the tools: taskmaster checks them before buying for Dorhum's and
  Nezhiri's tasks, but not Zasele's. On 2026-11-22 the tools were still in
  the vault from the day before. The marathon bought stock, paid Zasele for a
  knitted outfit task, and then stopped at sew's first step: "You seem to be
  missing: knitting needles".

  When nothing for the marathon is stashed there's no trip anywhere, and
  what's in the Eddy needs none either.
  Unstash needs empty hands: if yours are full and tools are stashed, it says
  so and this stops before starting taskmaster. With your hands full it
  doesn't combine anything either.

  The marathon alias runs this. Anything after it goes on to taskmaster.
  Typing ;taskmaster marathon yourself skips all this.

  Usage:
    ;start_marathon
=end

require 'yaml'

# What's stashed right now, written by ;stash (the same file ;unstash reads)
STASH_LIST = File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, 'stash.yaml')

# The stock the marathon sews and knits from (the same as unstash.lic's)
MARATHON_STOCK = /\b(?:burlap cloth|rat-pelt leather|wool yarn|cotton thread)$/i

# That stock as taskmaster and sew ask for it
MARATHON_PIECES = ['burlap cloth', 'rat leather', 'wool yarn', 'cotton thread'].freeze

# Pieces of one stock combined at most, so an odd reply can't keep it going
MARATHON_MOST_PIECES = 40

# COMBINE: "You combine the spools of thread together." (yarn too), "You must
# be holding both substances to combine them.", "Those items cannot be
# combined.", and past 400 yards of yarn or thread "The spool is not large
# enough to combine both threads." (2026-11-26; unmatched, it waited 15
# seconds and called it no reply)
MARATHON_COMBINED = /^You combine/
MARATHON_NOT_COMBINED = [/^You must/, /cannot be combined/, /^You can't/, /^What were you referring to/, /too (?:big|large|much|many)/i,
                         /^The spool is not large enough/].freeze

# The other scripts' methods are shared with this one while they run (see
# trash-sort's ask_vault), so none of these are named like ;unstash's.

# What ;unstash marathon gets back: the outfitting tools and supplies, and
# the marathon's stock
def stashed_for_marathon
  entries = File.exist?(STASH_LIST) ? YAML.safe_load(File.read(STASH_LIST)) || [] : []
  entries.select do |entry|
    entry['for'].to_a.include?('outfitting') && (entry['kind'] != 'materials' || entry['name'].to_s.match?(MARATHON_STOCK))
  end
end

# Just the tools and supplies, which the marathon can't start without
def stashed_outfitting_gear
  stashed_for_marathon.reject { |entry| entry['kind'] == 'materials' }
end

# "knitting needles, wool yarn (9)"
def list_stashed(entries)
  entries.map { |entry| entry['item'] || entry['name'] }.tally
         .map { |name, count| count > 1 ? "#{name} (#{count})" : name }.join(', ')
end

# "knitting needles, outfitting logbook, and one piece each of wool yarn and
# burlap cloth (the rest are thrown out)"
def list_trip(entries)
  stock, gear = entries.partition { |entry| entry['kind'] == 'materials' }
  parts = gear.empty? ? [] : [list_stashed(gear)]
  names = stock.map { |entry| entry['name'] }.uniq
  parts << "one piece each of #{names.join(', ')} (the rest are thrown out)" unless names.empty?
  parts.join(', and ')
end

# "your Eddy", "the vault", or "your Eddy and the vault": where ;stash put these
def marathon_stashed_where(entries)
  entries.map { |entry| entry['in'] == 'eddy' ? 'your Eddy' : 'the vault' }.uniq.sort.join(' and ')
end

def marathon_hands
  [DRC.right_hand, DRC.left_hand].compact.size
end

# The hand display can lag the game text by a moment
def marathon_holding?(count)
  10.times do
    return true if marathon_hands == count

    pause 0.1
  end
  false
end

# Takes one more piece of a stock out of the bag. The hands tell whether it
# came: get_item? would take the piece already held for it.
def take_piece?(stock, bag)
  held = marathon_hands
  DRC.bput("get my #{stock} from my #{bag}", /^You get/, /^What were you referring to/, /^I could not find/, /^You need a free hand/, /^You can't/) =~ /^You get/ &&
    marathon_holding?(held + 1)
end

# Combines a stock's pieces in the bag into one. Returns how many it put
# together, 0 if there weren't two, or nil if one is stuck in your hands.
def combine_pieces(stock, bag)
  return 0 unless take_piece?(stock, bag)

  pieces = 1
  while pieces < MARATHON_MOST_PIECES && take_piece?(stock, bag)
    reply = DRC.bput("combine #{stock.split.last}", MARATHON_COMBINED, *MARATHON_NOT_COMBINED)
    unless reply =~ MARATHON_COMBINED && marathon_holding?(1)
      DRC.message("start_marathon: couldn't combine the #{stock}: #{reply.empty? ? 'no reply' : reply}")
      break
    end
    pieces += 1
  end
  2.times { DRCI.put_away_item?(stock, bag) unless marathon_hands.zero? }
  return nil unless marathon_holding?(0)

  pieces > 1 ? pieces : 0
end

# Combines all four stocks. Returns false if a piece is stuck in your hands.
def combine_marathon_stock(bag)
  return true unless marathon_hands.zero?

  combined = {}
  MARATHON_PIECES.each do |stock|
    pieces = combine_pieces(stock, bag)
    if pieces.nil?
      DRC.message("start_marathon: couldn't put the #{stock} back in your #{bag}. Not starting the marathon with it in your hands.")
      return false
    end
    combined[stock] = pieces if pieces.positive?
  end
  unless combined.empty?
    DRC.message("start_marathon: combined into one each: #{combined.map { |stock, pieces| "#{stock} (#{pieces} pieces)" }.join(', ')}")
  end
  true
end

if Script.running?('taskmaster')
  DRC.message('start_marathon: taskmaster is already running.')
  exit
end

bag = get_settings.crafting_container
stashed = stashed_for_marathon
if stashed.empty?
  exit unless combine_marathon_stock(bag)
else
  DRC.message("start_marathon: getting these from #{marathon_stashed_where(stashed)} first: #{list_trip(stashed)}")
  DRC.wait_for_script_to_complete('unstash', ['marathon'])
  exit unless combine_marathon_stock(bag)

  stashed = stashed_for_marathon
  tools = stashed_outfitting_gear
  unless tools.empty?
    DRC.message("start_marathon: still in #{marathon_stashed_where(tools)}: #{list_stashed(tools)}. Not starting the marathon without them. " \
                'Run ;unstash outfitting (with empty hands), then marathon again.')
    exit
  end
  DRC.message("start_marathon: still in #{marathon_stashed_where(stashed)}, so taskmaster buys what it's short of: #{list_stashed(stashed)}") unless stashed.empty?
end

# Started on its own, as if typed, so ;kill taskmaster and ;stop_marathon
# work on it as usual and this script is done
start_script('taskmaster', ['marathon', *Script.current.vars[1..]])
